Falsifies `system_tests::user::net_confinement_tests::a_socket_moves_by_its_capability_and_a_closed_one_reaches_nothing`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect is a `CLOSE` that does not unbind: `net_stack` answers it `REP_OK` and keeps the socket,
its badge and its page in its table. §255 (each socket is its own capability) says close unbinds the
badge so a stale capability reaches nothing; with this patch every copy of a closed socket's
capability goes on reaching the socket.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(stale[0], NET_CLIENT_OK, "a copy of a closed socket's capability
still reached a socket: ...")`. Confirmed red on 2026-10-07 (UTC) at
`system_tests/src/user/net_confinement_tests.rs:275` on aarch64, with `script/test --arch aarch64
--test a_socket_moves_by`: the giver's copy answered its probe (`0xe0b2`). The hunk is portable
code, so one patch serves every leg; riscv64 and x86_64 were not replayed by hand.

